# Kanban Board

File-based task tracking for {{ .vars.campaign_name }}.

## Directory Structure

```
kanban/
├── README.md           # This file
├── todo/               # Tasks waiting to be started
├── in-progress/        # Tasks currently being worked on
├── review/             # Tasks awaiting review
├── done/               # Completed tasks
└── blocked/            # Tasks blocked by dependencies
```

## Task Format

Each task is a markdown file with front matter:

```markdown
---
task: task-name
commission: parent-commission
priority: high|medium|low
agent: assigned-agent-id
created: 2024-01-15
updated: 2024-01-16
---

# Task Title

## Description
What needs to be done.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] Criterion 1
- [ ] Criterion 2

## Notes
Additional context.
```

## Task Lifecycle

```
todo/ → in-progress/ → review/ → done/
                ↓
            blocked/
```

### Moving Tasks

```bash
# Start working on a task
guild kanban move task-name in-progress

# Submit for review
guild kanban move task-name review

# Mark as complete
guild kanban move task-name done

# Block a task
guild kanban move task-name blocked --reason "Waiting for API"
```

## Commands

```bash
# List all tasks
guild kanban list

# List by column
guild kanban list --column todo
guild kanban list --column in-progress

# Create new task
guild kanban create "Implement auth" --commission user-auth

# View task details
guild kanban show task-name

# Update priority
guild kanban priority task-name high
```

## Priority Levels

| Priority | Description | SLA |
|----------|-------------|-----|
| **high** | Critical, blocking other work | Complete ASAP |
| **medium** | Important, normal priority | Within sprint |
| **low** | Nice to have | When time permits |

## Best Practices

### Keep Tasks Small
- Each task should be completable in one session
- Break large tasks into subtasks
- Clear, specific acceptance criteria

### One Agent, One Task
- Each in-progress task should have one assigned agent
- Prevents conflicts and confusion
- Clear ownership

### Move Tasks Promptly
- Update status as work progresses
- Don't let tasks linger in wrong column
- Keeps the board accurate

### Document Blockers
When moving to blocked/:
```bash
guild kanban move task-name blocked --reason "Waiting for database credentials"
```

## Automation

Tasks are automatically:
- Created when commissions are decomposed
- Moved based on agent status updates
- Archived after completion

## Integration

The kanban board integrates with:
- **Commissions**: Tasks link back to parent commission
- **Agents**: Assigned agent tracked
- **Archives**: Completed tasks archived for reference

